{"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/EditorInspector\/editedObjectChanged","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/EditorInspector\/objectIdSelected","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/EditorInspector\/propertyDeleted","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/EditorInspector\/propertyEdited","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/EditorInspector\/propertyKeyed","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/EditorInspector\/propertySelected","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/EditorInspector\/propertyToggled","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/EditorInspector\/resourceSelected","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/EditorInspector\/restartRequested"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/EditorInspector\/edit(object:)","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/EditorInspector\/getEditedObject()","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/EditorInspector\/getSelectedPath()"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Properties","title":"Type Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/EditorInspector\/godotClassName"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Methods","title":"Type Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/EditorInspector\/instantiatePropertyEditor(object:type:path:hint:hintText:usage:wide:)"]}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EditorInspector","kind":"identifier"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This is the control that implements property editing in the editor’s Settings dialogs, the Inspector dock, etc. To get the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/EditorInspector","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" used in the editor’s Inspector dock, use ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/EditorInterface\/getInspector()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/EditorInspector"},{"text":" will show properties in the same order as the array returned by ","type":"text"},{"code":"Object\/getPropertyList()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If a property’s name is path-like (i.e. if it contains forward slashes), ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/EditorInspector","type":"reference"},{"text":" will create nested sections for “directories” along the path. For example, if a property is named ","type":"text"},{"code":"highlighting\/gdscript\/node_path_color","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", it will be shown as “Node Path Color” inside the “GDScript” section nested inside the “Highlighting” section.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If a property has ","type":"text"},{"code":"PropertyUsageFlags\/propertyUsageGroup","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" usage, it will group subsequent properties whose name starts with the property’s hint string. The group ends when a property does not start with that hint string or when a new group starts. An empty group name effectively ends the current group. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/EditorInspector","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" will create a top-level section for each group. For example, if a property with group usage is named ","type":"text"},{"code":"Collide With","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and its hint string is ","type":"text"},{"code":"collide_with_","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a subsequent ","type":"text"},{"code":"collide_with_area","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property will be shown as “Area” inside the “Collide With” section. There is also a special case: when the hint string contains the name of a property, that property is grouped too. This is mainly to help grouping properties like ","type":"text"},{"code":"font","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"font_color","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"font_size","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (using the hint string ","type":"text"},{"code":"font_","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If a property has ","type":"text"},{"code":"PropertyUsageFlags\/propertyUsageSubgroup","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" usage, a subgroup will be created in the same way as a group, and a second-level section will be created for each subgroup.","type":"text"}]},{"name":"Note","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Unlike sections created from path-like property names, "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/EditorInspector","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" won’t capitalize the name for sections created from groups. So properties with group usage usually use capitalized names instead of snake_cased names."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This object emits the following signals:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/EditorInspector\/propertySelected"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Edit